<title>UK: Nicaragua is latest member of world coffee pact.</title>
<headline>Nicaragua is latest member of world coffee pact.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nicaragua has signed up as a member of the International Coffee Agreement, bringing the number of signatories to the producer-consumer accord to 62.</p>
<p>Celsius Lodder, executive director of the International Coffee Organization (ICO), which administers the the pact, said on Thursday Nicaragua acceded to the 1994 agreement on March 24.</p>
<p>The London-based ICO now comprises 44 exporting and 18 importing member states. Exporting members account for around 95 percent of the world's coffee exports.</p>
<p>Nicaragua is an exporter of mild arabicas, with an average annual production over the last five years of around 725,000 bags.</p>
<p>It exported some 900,000 bags in 1995/96 coffee year. -- Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
